<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">formation</ansi>

Your company stands in a 3x3 formation: three <ansi fg="yellow">columns</ansi> (1 to 3, left to
right) and three <ansi fg="yellow">rows</ansi> (row 1 is the front, row 3 the back). Enemy groups
stand in a formation too, arranged for them: their toughest stand in front.

Where everyone stands decides who can strike whom.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">formation</ansi>
  Show your company's formation, and anyone not yet placed in it.

  <ansi fg="command">formation move [member] [row] [col]</ansi> - e.g. <ansi fg="command">formation move #1 1 2</ansi>
  Place a member. A member is <ansi fg="command">me</ansi> (you), a companion's number (<ansi fg="command">#1</ansi>), or a
  companion's name.

  <ansi fg="command">formation swap [member] [member]</ansi>
  Swap two members' places.

  <ansi fg="command">formation clear [member]</ansi>
  Take a member out of the formation.

  <ansi fg="command">formation reach [member]</ansi>
  In a fight, name the enemies that member can strike right now. Out of a
  fight, it shows how reach works within your own company.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Reach</ansi>

A fighter can strike a column of the other side only if it is their own
column or the one beside it. Column 1 can reach columns 1 and 2, but not 3.

How deep into that column they can strike depends on their weapon:

- <ansi fg="yellow">Plain melee</ansi> (swords, axes, fists): only the frontmost fighter standing
  in that column.
- <ansi fg="yellow">Reach</ansi> (weapons with reach, like polearms, and some beasts): the
  frontmost fighter, or the one just behind them.
- <ansi fg="yellow">Ranged</ansi> (bows, slings): anyone in the column, however deep.

When a front fighter falls, the one behind them becomes the frontmost, and
can be struck.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Interception</ansi>

A blow aimed at someone behind the front row is caught by the fighter in
the front row of the same column, if that fighter is alive.
Put your toughest in front to shield the rest. Your company does this for
you, and the enemy does it to you. Keep healers and casters behind them:
a blow that draws blood may break a chant (<ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>).
A foe's wound-up blow, such as the forest ogre's Crushing Blow, is caught
by the front row like any other, so keep your frail out of an ogre's
reach behind your toughest.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Guardians</ansi>

A guardian steps in front of its ward to take a blow meant for them, but
only from the ward's column or the next one (<ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>). <ansi fg="command">formation</ansi>
warns you, after a move, when a guardian stands too far from its ward:
"Out of reach: Tamsin Reed can't step in for you from there."

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Unplaced members</ansi>

A member not placed in the formation has no place to shield or be shielded
from. They can strike any enemy, and any enemy can strike them.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">In a fight</ansi>

If your target is out of your reach, you turn toward another your strategy
picks among those you can reach, and are told so: "You can't reach the
bandit captain from here. You turn toward the bandit cutthroat." See
<ansi fg="command">help targeting</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>.

Set your formation up before a fight: it's where everyone stands when the
blows begin, and it can't be changed during a battle (reading it, and
<ansi fg="command">formation reach</ansi>, still work).

In the web client, the Combat tab draws your formation; click a member
to move them (<ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>).
